{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 26, :comments ["<b>and his retinue.</b> As its Targum renders: וְסִיעַת מֵרַחֲמוֹהִי — the retinue of those who love him. And some interpret מֵרֵעֵהוּ with a mem at the root of the word, as in ״שְׁלֹשִׁים מֵרֵעִים״ of Samson, so that the phrase וַאֲחֻזַת would form a connected construct. But it is not the way of dignified speech to speak thus of royalty — 'the retinue of those who love him' — for if so, the entire retinue of those who love him he brought with him, and he would have had only one retinue of friends. Therefore it should be interpreted according to the first reading. And do not be astonished at the tav of אֲחֻזַת — even though there is no governing noun in construct — there is a parallel in Scripture: ״עֶזְרָת מִצָּר״ (Psalms 60), and ״שְׁכֻרַת וְלֹא מִיָּיִן״ (Isaiah 51)." "<b>Retinue.</b> A term for a band and a group — those held together."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:00:42.766330965Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}